row(29, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THEY WILL SAY: BECAUSE THEY FORSOOK THE COVENANT OF THE LORD, THE GOD OF THEIR FATHERS, WHICH HE MADE WITH THEM WHEN HE BROUGHT THEM OUT OF THE LAND OF EGYPT. {HP(29, 24, (("על", "אשר", "עזבו", "את", "ברית", "יהוה"), "because they forsook the covenant of the LORD — the fifth covenant of the chapter (the ink: ten in 29 and 31, never in 30)"), (("בהוציאו", "אתם", "מארץ", "מצרים"), "when He brought them out of the land of Egypt — the covenant DATED to the going out"))} {AP(29, 24, (("על", "דשבקו", "ית", "קימא", "דיי"), "because they abandoned the covenant of the LORD"), (("באפקותיה", "יתהון", "מארעא", "דמצרים"), "when He brought them out of the land of Egypt"))} THE ANSWER\'S FIRST HALF — forsaking the covenant. Fresh.')
row(29, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THEY WENT AND SERVED OTHER GODS AND BOWED DOWN TO THEM — GODS THEY HAD NOT KNOWN AND WHO HAD NOT APPORTIONED TO THEM. {HP(29, 25, (("וילכו", "ויעבדו", "אלהים", "אחרים"), "and they went and served other gods — other gods nineteen in the Torah (the ink)"), (("וישתחוו", "להם"), "and bowed to them"), (("אלהים", "אשר", "לא", "ידעום", "ולא", "חלק", "להם"), "gods they had not known and who had not APPORTIONED to them — 148:8\'s row reads it by 4:19\'s allotting (the outside row)"))} {AP(29, 25, (("ופלחו", "לטעות", "עממיא"), "and served THE ERRORS OF THE PEOPLES — other gods rendered so"), (("דחלן", "די", "לא", "ידענון"), "FEARS (dachalan) they had not known — the gods rendered objects of fear"), (("ולא", "אוטיבא", "להון"), "and who DID NO GOOD to them — apportioned (chalak) rendered benefited"))} Onkelos writes the meaning three times — the errors, the fears, did no good for the hard apportioned. Fresh.')
row(29, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE ANGER OF THE LORD BURNED AGAINST THAT LAND, TO BRING ON IT ALL THE CURSE WRITTEN IN THIS BOOK. {HP(29, 26, (("ויחר", "אף", "יהוה", "בארץ", "ההוא"), "and the LORD\'s anger burned against that land — the land the object"), (("את", "כל", "הקללה", "הכתובה", "בספר", "הזה"), "all the curse written in this book — 29:19\'s twin (the ink: each other\'s kin); the curse singular (kelalah), 28:15\'s word"))} {AP(29, 26, (("ותקף", "רגזא", "דיי"), "and the LORD\'s anger grew strong"), (("כל", "לוטיא", "דכתיבין", "בספרא", "הדין"), "all the curses written in this book — the singular\'s plural"))} The land\'s curse and the man\'s (29:19) the same clause — the written curse\'s two scopes, individual and national. Fresh.')
row(29, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LORD UPROOTED THEM FROM THEIR LAND IN ANGER, WRATH AND GREAT FURY, AND CAST THEM INTO ANOTHER LAND, AS THIS DAY. {HP(29, 27, (("ויתשם", "יהוה", "מעל", "אדמתם"), "and the LORD uprooted them from their soil — 43:29\'s row (the outside row on this verse)"), (("באף", "ובחמה", "ובקצף", "גדול"), "in anger and in wrath and in great fury — the three"), (("וישלכם", "אל", "ארץ", "אחרת", "כיום", "הזה"), "and cast them into another land as this day — as this day the exile written as present"))} {AP(29, 27, (("וטלטלנון", "יי", "מעל", "ארעהון"), "and the LORD CAST THEM ABOUT from their land — uprooted rendered made wander (taltel)"), (("ואגלנון", "לארעא", "אחרי"), "and EXILED them to another land — cast rendered exiled (agli); sitting 18\'s exile for lead again"))} The export\'s Aramaic carries a parenthesized variant for wrath (not cut). Fresh.')
row(29, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'THE HIDDEN THINGS ARE THE LORD OUR GOD\'S; THE REVEALED ARE OURS AND OUR CHILDREN\'S FOREVER, TO DO ALL THE WORDS OF THIS LAW. {HP(29, 28, (("הנסתרת", "ליהוה", "אלהינו"), "the hidden things are the LORD our God\'s — ONCE in the Bible (the ink)"), (("והנגלת", "לנו", "ולבנינו", "עד", "עולם"), "and the revealed to us and to our children forever"), (("לעשות", "את", "כל", "דברי", "התורה", "הזאת"), "to do all the words of this law — six in order with 28:58 and 31:12 (the ink\'s kin)"))} {AP(29, 28, (("דמטמרן", "קדם", "יי", "אלהנא"), "THE HIDDEN are BEFORE the LORD our God — to rendered before (kodam); hidden (mitamran) here and 33:19 (the ink)"), (("ודמגלין", "לנא", "ולבננא"), "and the revealed to us and to our children"))} THE CHAPTER\'S CLOSE — the hidden and the revealed the compile\'s boundary: the revealed the code\'s domain (DV29-05). Fresh.')
